.TH SHEDMAN-UPDATE 1 "2026-04-25" "ShedOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shedman-update \- interactive ShedOS upgrade flow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shedman update
.RB [ -y | --yes ]
.RB [ -h | --help ]
.br
.B shedman update
.RB { -l | --list-snapshots }
.br
.B shedman update
.RB { -r | --rollback }
.RI [ N ]
.br
.B shedman update --history
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shedman update
is the primary upgrade command on ShedOS. It wraps three steps in
one interactive flow, bracketed by a snapper pre/post btrfs
snapshot pair:
.IP \(bu 2
.B pacman -Syu
\(em official repo updates.
.IP \(bu 2
.B yay -Sua
\(em AUR updates (if
.B yay
is installed).
.IP \(bu 2
.B shedman config --sync
\(em 3-way merge of dotfiles in $HOME against packaged defaults.
.PP
Every step is gated by an explicit y/N prompt; nothing destructive
runs without confirmation. The snapper snapshots make every upgrade
reversible via
.B shedman rollback
or
.BR "shedman update --rollback" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -y , " --yes"
Unattended mode. Pass
.B --noconfirm
to pacman/yay and
.B --yes
to
.BR "shedman config --sync" .
Conflicts still drop
.I .shedosnew
files instead of overwriting your edits — there is no silent data
loss path.
.TP
.BR -l , " --list-snapshots"
Print the recent snapper snapshot list and exit. Use this to find a
pre-upgrade snapshot number for
.B --rollback.
.TP
.BR -r " " \fIN\fR ", " --rollback " " \fIN\fR
Roll back the root subvolume to snapshot
.IR N .
If
.I N
is omitted, you'll be prompted from the recent list. Reboot is
required after the call returns.
.TP
.B --history
Open the upgrade-history TUI (delegates to
.BR shedman-upgrade-history (1)
\(em an internal helper).
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/shedos/system.toml
Read by
.B shedman config --sync
during the post-upgrade dotfile pass.
.TP
.I /var/lib/shedos/
Last-seen + baseline state for the dotfile sync.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shedman (1),
.BR shedman-config (1),
.BR shedman-rollback (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR yay (8).
